# Figma selection → Delivery Checkout V1

When the user provides a **Figma selection** (URL + optional CSS) for the delivery-checkout-v1 page:

## 1. Parse the selection

- **URL**: `https://www.figma.com/design/re5Fauw1m9dJxYlIdR8Btn/...?node-id=2362-XXXXX`
- **fileKey**: `re5Fauw1m9dJxYlIdR8Btn`
- **nodeId**: From `node-id=2362-XXXXX` → use `2362:XXXXX` (colon) for Figma MCP

## 2. Fetch design

- Call `mcp_Figma_get_design_context` and `mcp_Figma_get_screenshot` for that `fileKey` and `nodeId` to get structure and visuals.

## 3. Place in the right order

Sections are ordered by **ascending Figma node ID**. Current order (see comment in `DeliveryCheckoutV1.jsx`):

| Order | Node ID   | Section id / slug        |
|-------|-----------|---------------------------|
| 1     | 2362:17118 | (header)                  |
| 2     | 2362:17126 | delivery-title           |
| 3     | 2362:17133 | problem                  |
| 4     | 2362:17136 | why-problem (in bg layer) |
| 5     | 2362:17139 | breaking-down (in bg)     |
| 6     | 2362:17144 | opportunity              |
| 7     | 2362:17175 | things-working            |

- **Insert** the new section between the two existing sections whose node IDs it falls between. If the user says "after X" or "before Y", use that; otherwise use node ID order.
- Use class `dc-v1-gap` on the section so the 80px gap between sections is applied.

## 4. Implement

- Add the section in `DeliveryCheckoutV1.jsx`: wrapper with `data-node-id="2362:XXXXX"`, semantic HTML, and apply any user-given CSS (e.g. `display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 32px`) on the **inner** container (e.g. `.dc-v1-<slug>-inner`).
- Add styles in `DeliveryCheckoutV1.css` with prefix `dc-v1-` and a slug derived from the section (e.g. `dc-v1-things-working`). Include responsive padding in existing media queries where appropriate.
- Add `{ id: '<section-id>', title: '<Menu title>' }` to the `sections` array so the section appears in the Menu.

## 5. Images

- If the selection contains exportable images: add the node to `scripts/export-figma-delivery-checkout-v1-images.js` (id, idKey, file name in `public/images/delivery-checkout-v1/`). Use `process.env.PUBLIC_URL + '/images/delivery-checkout-v1/<file>.png'` and an `onError` placeholder in the component.

## 6. Page layout rules (unchanged)

- Page: full width, no outer padding; inner content uses `max-width: 1200px` (or 1176px where specified), `margin: 0 auto`, `padding: 0 24px` (or 16px/12px in media queries).
- Between sections: 80px gap (`.dc-v1-gap`).
